Privacy Policy for "Simple Repeat Alarm"

Effective date: October 25, 2026

This app stores your alarm settings only on your device. It does not send your alarms or personal information to any server run by the developer.

1. Advertising
This app uses Google AdMob, an advertising service provided by Google LLC. To serve ads, measure their performance and prevent fraud, Google may collect:
- the advertising identifier (IDFA, only if you allow tracking) and identifiers limited to the app or developer
- approximate location estimated from your IP address
- device information such as model and OS version
- information about ads shown and your interactions with ads and the app
- crash and performance information
For how Google handles this information, see:
- Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
- How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

2. Permission to track (App Tracking Transparency)
The app may ask for permission to use the advertising identifier to show more relevant ads. You can use every feature of the app without allowing it. You can change this at any time in iPhone Settings > Privacy & Security > Tracking, or in the app's Settings > Open Tracking Settings.

3. Consent in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland
In these regions, the app asks for your consent to use information for advertising through Google's consent management. You can change your choices at any time in the app's Settings > Privacy Settings.

4. Notifications and alarms
The app asks for permission to send notifications so that alarms ring on time. On iOS 26.1 and later, it may ask for permission to use alarms so they ring even in Silent mode or Focus. The developer does not collect any information through these permissions.

5. Information stored on your device
Your alarm times, names, sounds and repeat settings, and app usage such as how many times alarms have rung (used to decide when to ask for a review) are stored only on your device. They are deleted when you delete the app.

6. Changes
If this policy changes, we will post the update on this page.

